---
/**
 * Confidentialité : le site (aucun cookie, aucune mesure d'audience, journaux de l'hébergeur), l'app desktop (pas de
 * compte, données locales, aucune télémétrie, connexions choisies), les droits RGPD.
 */
import LegalDoc from "@/layouts/LegalDoc.astro";
import { LINKS } from "@/lib/site";
---

<LegalDoc
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="The TaskForce website uses no cookies and no analytics. The desktop app has no account, keeps your data on your computer and sends us nothing."
  updated="19 October 2026"
>
  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and runs <strong>no analytics</strong> or advertising trackers.</li>
    <li>The desktop app has <strong>no account</strong>. Your data stays on your computer, and the app sends us nothing.</li>
    <li>The services you connect to the app receive data directly from your computer, under their own terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Pierre Michel, the publisher of TaskForce (see the <a href="/legal/notice">legal notice</a>), is responsible for
    the processing described here. For any question about your data, write to{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting.</strong> Vercel, our host, processes technical data such as your IP address and browser
      details to serve the pages and protect the site from abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts and images</strong> are served by this site itself: no request goes to a third party while you
      read.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Downloads</strong> are served by GitHub from the project's releases. When you download a file, GitHub
      receives the request, under GitHub's privacy statement.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email.</strong> If you write to us, we use your address and your message only to answer you, and we
      delete them once they are no longer needed.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The desktop app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your data stays on your computer.</strong> Projects, Brain OS pages, attachments and settings are kept
      in the app's data folder. We have no access to them.
    </li>
    <li><strong>No telemetry.</strong> The app sends no usage data, to us or to anyone else.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connections you choose.</strong> When you add an AI provider's API key, start Claude Code, or connect
      GitHub, Copilot, MCP servers, Plane or webhooks, the data they need goes from your computer straight to that
      service, under its own terms and privacy policy. We are never in between.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Updates.</strong> The app asks GitHub whether a new version exists, so GitHub receives that request.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The web app</h2>
  <p>
    Until it closes, the hosted web app at app.taskforce-project.fr is covered by its own privacy policy, shown in the
    app. To take your projects with you, see <a href="/migrate">moving from the web app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you can access, correct, delete or export the personal data we hold about you, and object to or
    restrict its processing. Write to <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a>. You can also lodge a
    complaint with your data protection authority: in France, the CNIL (cnil.fr).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we update it on this page and change the date above.</p>
</LegalDoc>
